<Base title="Index methodology — ClaimClock"><div class="wrap narrow prose"><p class="eyebrow">READ THE NUMBERS CAREFULLY</p><h1>How we read NL-48 / आँकड़ों का तरीका</h1><p>NL-48 is an insurer's public disclosure of health-service turnaround times. We transcribe the published cashless pre-authorisation and discharge buckets for each TPA and for individual/group policies. These are the insurer's reported figures, not a patient survey or an independent compliance audit.</p><p>NL-48 बीमा कंपनी का प्रकाशित खुलासा है। हम हर TPA तथा व्यक्तिगत/समूह पॉलिसी के प्रकाशित समय-खंड दिखाते हैं। यह स्वतंत्र नियम-पालन जाँच नहीं है।</p><h2>What this does and does not show</h2><ul><li>The 2–6 hour bucket straddles the three-hour discharge deadline. We do not estimate the share decided before or after three hours.</li><li>The disclosure clock starts when the TPA receives the discharge bill. Family-entered submission times may capture a different point.</li><li>Rows with different TPAs, periods, policy types or units are not combined. Percentages are copied without renormalising rounding.</li><li>A sample size is shown only when the exact cashless denominator is identifiable. A missing denominator is not zero.</li><li>Missing, scanned, malformed and inconsistent filings are tracked explicitly. Coverage is incomplete and has no market-wide ranking.</li><li>Patient reports are voluntary and unverified. Every published cell must contain at least ten reports. Small cells, individual timestamps and hospital names are never displayed.</li></ul><h2>Audit the dataset</h2><p>Each row records its source URL, PDF page, insurer, TPA, period, unit and retrieval date. The repository contains a reproducible transcription pipeline, source hashes, exclusions and spot-check evidence.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button-secondary" href="/data/nl48.csv" download>CSV ↓</a><a class="button-secondary" href="/data/nl48.json" download>JSON ↓</a><a href="/data/filings.json">Coverage register ↗</a></div><p><a href="https://github.com/ketan952/claimclock/blob/main/research/nl48-methodology.md">Detailed source methodology and QA ↗</a></p><h2 data-i18n="sources.title">Primary sources behind letter links</h2><p data-i18n="sources.body">Short links in your letters redirect to these original IRDAI documents.</p>{sourceLinks.map(source=><details><summary data-i18n={`sources.${source.slug}`}>{source.title_en}</summary><a class="source-url" href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.url}</a><p><a href={`/s/${source.slug}`}>/s/{source.slug}</a> · 302</p></details>)}<h2>Corrections</h2><p>Open a source-linked issue in the public repository. Do not put policy numbers, medical records or personal details in public issues. Contact verification means the detail was found on a primary-source page; it does not mean a call was made or an inbox tested.</p></div></Base>
